<title>PERU: Peru's Q1 wheat output falls 66 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's Q1 wheat output falls 66 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's first-quarter wheat production fell 66 percent to 701 tonnes from 2,087 tonnes in the same period last year, Agriculture Ministry said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Wheat imports in the first three months dropped by 31 percent to $42.6 million, from $61.6 million in the same period last year, the report added.</p>
<p>Peru's wheat is grown mostly in the central and southeastern Andean regions.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
